 "notes": "Chart title reads \"CHART NINE\" (chart 9 of 16). Year header \"1939\" printed above the DATE label on the right (ledger) page; the facing left page (p.118) carries the printed annotations, the grid is p.119. Column groups left-to-right: U.S. STEEL, BETHLEHEM STEEL, KEY PRICE, each with SR/NR/UT/DT/NRC/SRC. Header carried-forward pivotal points: red Downward-Trend values (US 53 1/4, BS 60 1/4, KP 113 1/2, each black-underlined) sit one grid row above the blue Natural-Rally values (US 64 7/8, BS 75 1/2, KP 140 3/8) that share the \"1939\" line; both checksum (64 7/8+75 1/2=140 3/8; 53 1/4+60 1/4=113 1/2). Every complete dated row checksums (US+BS=KP) EXCEPT MAR22, where US 53 1/2 + BS 63 3/8 = 116 7/8 but KP is written 117 7/8 (genuine 1-point discrepancy; BS integer is partly obscured by a red gridline and could conceivably be 64 3/8, which would reconcile). No Sunday rows. April 7 (Good Friday, market closed) has no row: rows run ...6, SAT.8. All hand-drawn underlines are single and black (MAR9 NR pivots, APR11 DT reaction lows, SAT15 NR rally, and the three header DT values). Ink convention holds: UT would be black, DT red, and the other four columns blue pencil. The MAR30 annotation contains an original typographical omission ('being a lower than' \u2014 the word 'price' is missing, present in the parallel MAR31 sentence); transcribed verbatim.",
